      "data": {
        "text": "**Selecting the Provider**\n\nI've decided to move forward with the Google Cloud Speech-to-Text API. This choice feels right, and it allows me to start sketching out the `poll_transcription.py ` structure. I'm focusing on how I'll integrate the API calls and handle potential errors during the polling process.\n\n\n**Defining the Core Structure**\n\nI'm now fully committed to the Google Cloud Speech-to-Text API and the `poll_transcription.py` script. The structure is taking shape, with the core functions outlined. The next step is a deep dive into the Google Cloud client library integration and crafting the polling loop with the `get_operation` method, handling various job states and error scenarios. I'll need to work on the function signature and handle the returned results.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789819128922,
          "start": 1789819127135
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b988855f001qPxGJxpyuC0lAC",
      "message_id": "msg_0b9887f6f001mm3vRXO8QrhMIo",
      "session_id": "ses_f467780a7ffeAzPHm43eF4sZLV",
      "time_created": 1789819127135,
      "time_updated": 1789819128923
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "tqqaMMiSWpnOk40p",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "from google.cloud import speech_v1p1beta1 as speech\nfrom google.api_core.operation import Operation\n\ndef poll_transcription_job(operation_name: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Polls a transcription job and returns the transcript.\n\n    Args:\n        operation_name: The name of the long-running operation (job ID).\n\n    Returns:\n        The transcribed text if the job is completed, otherwise an empty string.\n    \"\"\"\n    client = speech.SpeechClient()\n\n    operation: Operation = client.long_running_recognize(\n        operation_name=operation_name\n    )\n\n    result = operation.result()\n\n    transcript_parts = []\n    for result in result.results:\n        for alternative in result.alternatives:\n            transcript_parts.append(alternative.transcript)\n\n    return \" \".join(transcript_parts)\n",
            "filePath": "poll_transcription.py"
          },
          "metadata": {
